<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2020/06/apple-watch-10-titanium-finishes-crown.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="brief" align="left" style="float:left;margin:0 20px 20px 0;width:160px;height:auto;" />Prior to watchOS 27, the easiest way to force quit Apple Watch apps was by swiping across them in the App Switcher screen, but that's no longer possible because the Digital Crown double-click gesture that got you there is now <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/17/watchos-27-removes-useful-apple-watch-feature/">reserved</a> for Apple's upcoming Live Rewind AI feature. Fortunately, there's still a way to force quit apps in watchOS 27.<br/>
<br/>
